WHAT IT CHANGES
---------------
The serial result-aggregation loop in BSimProgramCorrelatorMatching.discoverPotentialMatches
(old lines 220-237) is replaced by two phases:

  PHASE A (serial, order-preserving): drain the ConcurrentQ results IN COLLECTION ORDER into
  discoveredMatches — byte-for-byte the same pair order the old loop produced — while grouping
  pairs into two per-role maps (node -> ArrayList<FunctionPair>). Cost: one map lookup + one
  list append per pair; no per-node HashMap rehash storms.

  PHASE B (parallel via ConcurrentQ/GThreadPool, matching the VT reference-correlator
  precedent of docs/decomp/ghidra-vt-optimization-2026-06-09.md): one work item per
  FunctionNode builds that node's entire associates map, pre-sized to its exact final entry
  count (new package-private FunctionNode.presizeAssociates), inserting in deterministic
  Phase A order.

